0,Huave language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Huave_language,"The Huave people of San Mateo del Mar, who call themselves Ikoots, meaning ""us"", refer to their language as ombeayiiüts, meaning ""our language"". In San Francisco del Mar, the corresponding terms are Kunajts (""us"") and umbeyajts (""our language""). The term ""Huave"" is thought to come from the Zapotec languages, meaning ""people who rot in the humidity"", according to the 17th-century Spanish ...","Huave, San Dionisio del Mar",Huavean
